I found an important claim-selection issue: selecting `SPEC.encrypt-entry` alone removes the separate `encrypt-loop` circularity that the entry proof needs, so the backend unrolls the symbolic loop indefinitely. That is not the candidate’s target command and is not a proof failure. I’m stopping this diagnostic run and will execute the actual complete `SPEC` module, where both positive claims are present together.
